      "type": "copy",
      "text": "Many brands go through identity crises, and Hot Topic was no exception. Thought to be a brand for goths and emos, it actually reaches a much broader audience. The challenge was to stay true to its DNA while evolving how it presented itself — creating campaigns that felt on brand while appealing to a large music fan base."
    },
